  "blocks": [
    {
      "blockId": "lin-geo-blk-1",
      "kind": "explanation",
      "heading": "Algebraic Conditions for Consistency",
      "content": "For system $a_1 x + b_1 y + c_1 = 0$ and $a_2 x + b_2 y + c_2 = 0$:\n1. $a_1/a_2 \\ne b_1/b_2$: Intersecting lines, unique solution (consistent).\n2. $a_1/a_2 = b_1/b_2 = c_1/c_2$: Coincident lines, infinitely many solutions (dependent consistent).\n3. $a_1/a_2 = b_1/b_2 \\ne c_1/c_2$: Parallel lines, no solution (inconsistent)."
    }
  ],
  "workedExamples": [
    {
      "prompt": "Check whether the pair of equations x + 3y = 6 and 2x - 3y = 12 is consistent.",
      "steps": [
        "Step 1: Write in standard form: x + 3y - 6 = 0 and 2x - 3y - 12 = 0.",
        "Step 2: a1/a2 = 1/2, b1/b2 = 3/(-3) = -1.",
        "Step 3: Since a1/a2 != b1/b2, the system has a unique solution and is consistent.",
        "Step 4: Adding the equations: 3x = 18 => x = 6. Then 6 + 3y = 6 => y = 0. Solution is (6, 0)."
      ],
      "answer": "Consistent with unique solution (6, 0)"
    }
  ],
